      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "90ef959705f0a32fc6e1d94b260bc9bb183017bab5763b221b7d5e8181c38f6f"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "We will consider the background polygenes to be completely additive, and assume that the background genetic value A is normally distributed with mean 0 and variance $ \\sigma_{A}^{2} $. The phenotypic value of an individual with major-locus genotype g and background polygenic value A is assumed to be normally distributed with mean $ \\mu_{g} + A $ and variance $ \\sigma_{E}^{2} $. Ignoring common-family effects, if the jth sib has background genetic value $ A_{o_{j}} $, the conditional likelihood for the jth sib in the ith family becomes",
      "source_page": 385,
      "printed_page": 365,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter13:p019:b12",
        "Genetics_chapter13:p020:b2"
      ],
